$$5x + 4y = 47$$
$$5x - 4y = 13$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, '6', ARRAY['6'], E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(5x + 4y) + (5x - 4y) = 47 + 13$, giving $10x = 60$, so $x = 6$. A common error is subtracting the equations instead of adding, which gives $8y = 34$ and $y = 4.25$, solving for $y$ rather than $x$. Another error is computing $10x = 60$ correctly but dividing by 5 instead of 10, yielding an incorrect value of 12.', NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 60, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-18"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-18","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);













